  "content": {
    "id": "p105-q1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": {
      "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
      "version": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "p105-q1-stem",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Which of the following are equations of a circle?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p105-q1-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x^2+y^2=8$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Circle.",
          "worked": "The equation has the form $x^2+y^2=r^2$, with $r^2=8>0$. It is a circle with centre $(0,0)$ and radius $2\\sqrt{2}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p105-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$x^2-y^2=8$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Not a circle.",
          "worked": "Not a circle. The coefficients of $x^2$ and $y^2$ have opposite signs; a circle's expanded equation has equal coefficients on these squared terms.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p105-q1-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$4x^2+4y^2=9$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Circle.",
          "worked": "Dividing by $4$ gives\n$$x^2+y^2=\\frac{9}{4}.$$\nIt is a circle with centre $(0,0)$ and radius $\\frac{3}{2}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p105-q1-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$9x^2+9y^2=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Circle.",
          "worked": "Dividing by $9$ gives\n$$x^2+y^2=\\frac{1}{9}.$$\nIt is a circle with centre $(0,0)$ and radius $\\frac{1}{3}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p105-q1-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$x^2+y^2=-2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Not a circle.",
          "worked": "Not a circle. For real $x$ and $y$, $x^2+y^2\\geq 0$, so the sum cannot equal $-2$. There are no real points.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p105-q1-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$3x^2+4y^2=5$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Not a circle.",
          "worked": "Not a circle. The coefficients of $x^2$ and $y^2$ are unequal, so the equation cannot be written in circle standard form by dividing through by a common coefficient.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p105-q1-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$(x+y)^2=4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Not a circle.",
          "worked": "Taking square roots gives $x+y=2$ or $x+y=-2$. These are two parallel straight lines, so the equation does not represent a circle.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p105-q1-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$x^2+y^2=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Degenerate circle.",
          "worked": "Both squares must be zero, giving $x=0$ and $y=0$. The graph is the single point $(0,0)$, called a degenerate circle with radius $0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p105-q1-i",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "i",
        "prompt": "$(x+y)^2+(x-y)^2=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Circle.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\nx^2+2xy+y^2+x^2-2xy+y^2&=1\\\\\n2x^2+2y^2&=1\\\\\nx^2+y^2&=\\frac{1}{2}.\n\\end{align*}$$\nIt is a circle with centre $(0,0)$ and radius $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p105-q1-j",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "j",
        "prompt": "$(x+y)^2-(x-y)^2=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Not a circle.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\nx^2+2xy+y^2-(x^2-2xy+y^2)&=1\\\\\n4xy&=1\\\\\nxy&=\\frac{1}{4}.\n\\end{align*}$$\nNot a circle. The squared terms cancel, leaving a product of $x$ and $y$ rather than the circle standard form.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p105-q1-k",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "k",
        "prompt": "$(x-1)(x-2)+(y-1)(y-2)=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p105-q1-k-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Circle.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p105-q1-k-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Complete the square to obtain ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\left(x-\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2+\\left(y-\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2=\\frac{1}{2}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Expand, then complete the square in both variables:\n$$\\begin{align*}\nx^2-3x+y^2-3y+4&=0\\\\\n\\left(x-\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2-\\frac{9}{4}+\\left(y-\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2-\\frac{9}{4}+4&=0\\\\\n\\left(x-\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2+\\left(y-\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2&=\\frac{1}{2}.\n\\end{align*}$$\nIt is a circle with centre $\\left(\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{3}{2}\\right)$ and radius $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      }
    ]
  },
